abstract: >-
  Machine-independent terminal configuration: a three-line status line for Claude Code (model,
  path, git state, pull request and toolchain; context, prompt cache, cost and rate-limit gauges;
  system load, host and clock), with Nerd Font, emoji or Unicode icons, a colour-blind-safe palette
  and a layout that follows the width of the terminal; a two-line blue powerline prompt for
  Starship that stays readable on light and dark terminals; a configuration of the terminal Ghostty
  for text and mathematics, in the colours of Tokyo Night with a readable dim colour, a light
  companion and a colour-blind-safe alternative pair, with two fonts of one width and measured
  contrasts; and a configuration of tmux with a quiet status line. Installers link everything into
  place, so that a git pull updates every machine, and never overwrite a per-machine file, edit a
  shell rc file or change the default terminal.
